===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Severne}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Sæfern}}, ultimately from {{der|en|cel-pro|*Sabrinā}} (compare {{cog|cy|Hafren}}), perhaps from {{m|cel-pro|*samaros||[[summer fallow]]}}. {{doublet|en|Sabrina}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛv.ə(ɹ)n/}}
* {{a|Aus}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsev.ən/}}
* {{a|US|Canada}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛv.ɚn/}}
* {{homophone|en|seven}} {{q|non-rhotic accents}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛvə(ɹ)n|s=2}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# A river of [[England]] and [[Wales]] that flows into the [[Bristol Channel]].
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XIX|32|There twice a day the '''Severn''' fills,<br>⁠The salt sea-water passes by,<br>⁠And hushes half the babbling Wye,<br>And makes a silence in the hills.}}
# {{place|en|long river|in northern|p/Ontario}} which flows into [[Hudson Bay]].
# {{place|en|short river|in central|p/Ontario}} which flows into [[Lake Huron]].
# A number of other rivers in [[Australia]], [[New Zealand]] and the [[United States]].
# {{place|en|township|p/Ontario|c/Canada}}, created in 1994 on the amalgamation of several smaller communities.
# {{place|en|census-designated place|co/Anne Arundel County|s/Maryland|c/USA}}.
# {{place|en|small town|co/Northampton County|s/North Carolina|c/USA}}.
# {{surname|en}}.

